        {
          "id": 1011234811,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "QString::compare was called more than once for the same values, leading to unnecessary calls. Additionally, the if-clause was not required as it already was covered with the comparison value and was just a shortcut for cmp != 0 in the alternate if-clause.\n\ncolumnString was called 3 times, after the patch it is only called 1, and columnString is expensive. And comparing two strings with == is costly, as it internally resolves to ::compare() == 0.\n\nNow to the memory consumption, the two subsequent calls to columnString will result in QString being casted internally which in turns is more memory being used. Now lessThan is a method called for each row individually, which results in huge memory consumption due to the unnecessary QString's for each time the method is called.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
